              "lower": "0",
              "upper": "1",
              "infinite": null,
              "description": "This parameter defines the maximal number of wait frames to be sent for a pending connection.",
              "metadata": {
                "RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF": "ECUC_FrArTp_00059",
                "LOWER-MULTIPLICITY": "0",
                "UPPER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "SCOPE": "LOCAL",
                "MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "ORIGIN": "AUTOSAR_ECUC",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-MULTIPLICITY": "true",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE": "true",
                "VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE": "false",
                "MAX": "255",
                "MIN": "0"
              },
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "name": "FrArTpStMin",
              "path": "/FrArTp/FrArTpMultipleConfig/FrArTpChannel/FrArTpStMin",
              "type": "ECUC-FLOAT-PARAM-DEF",
              "lower": "1",
              "upper": "1",
              "infinite": null,
              "description": "This parameter defines the minimum amount of time between two succeeding CFs of a 1:1 segmented transmission in seconds. Valid values are 0, 100µs, 200µs .. 900µs, 1ms, 2ms .. 127ms. The value can be changed at runtime using the FrArTp_ChangeParameter interface.",
              "metadata": {
                "INTRODUCTION": "FrArTpStMin must be an integer multiple of the cycle length multiplied with the multiplexing factor, i.e. FrArTpStMin = n * FrIfGdCycle * m, where n is an integer >= 0 and m is the cycle multiplexor of those cycles where PDUs of the PDU pool are scheduled. Please note: Due to the scheduling strategies of FrArTp, FrArTpStMin can only be kept to a degree defined by the maximum temporal distance of the PDUs of a PDU pool within one FlexRay cycle.",
                "RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF": "ECUC_FrArTp_00042",
                "LOWER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "UPPER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "SCOPE": "LOCAL",
                "ORIGIN": "AUTOSAR_ECUC",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE": "true",
                "VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE": "false",
                "MAX": "0.127",
                "MIN": "0"
              },
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "name": "FrArTpStMinGrpSeg",
              "path": "/FrArTp/FrArTpMultipleConfig/FrArTpChannel/FrArTpStMinGrpSeg",
              "type": "ECUC-FLOAT-PARAM-DEF",
              "lower": "0",
              "upper": "1",
              "infinite": null,
              "description": "This parameter defines the minimum amount of time between two succeeding CFs of a 1:n segmented transmission in seconds. Valid values are 0, 100µs, 200µs ... 900µs, 1ms, 2ms .. 127ms. The value can be changed at runtime using the FrArTp_ChangeParameter interface.",
              "metadata": {
                "INTRODUCTION": "FrArTpStMinGrpSeg must be an integer multiple of the cycle length multiplied with the multiplexing factor, i.e. FrArTpStMinGrpSeg = n * FrIfGdCycle * m, where n is an integer >= 0 and m is the cycle multiplexor of those cycles where PDUs of the PDU pool are scheduled. Please note: Due to the scheduling strategies of FrArTp, FrArTpStMinGrpSeg can only be kept to a degree defined by the maximum temporal distance of the PDUs of a PDU pool within one FlexRay cycle.",
                "RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF": "ECUC_FrArTp_00060",
                "LOWER-MULTIPLICITY": "0",
                "UPPER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "SCOPE": "LOCAL",
                "MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "ORIGIN": "AUTOSAR_ECUC",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-MULTIPLICITY": "true",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE": "true",
                "VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE": "false",
                "MAX": "0.127",
                "MIN": "0"
              },
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "name": "FrArTpTc",
              "path": "/FrArTp/FrArTpMultipleConfig/FrArTpChannel/FrArTpTc",
              "type": "ECUC-BOOLEAN-PARAM-DEF",
              "lower": "1",
              "upper": "1",
              "infinite": null,
              "description": "With this switch Transmit Cancellation and Receive Cancellation can be turned on or off for this channel.",
              "metadata": {
                "RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF": "ECUC_FrArTp_00043",
                "LOWER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "UPPER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "SCOPE": "LOCAL",
                "ORIGIN": "AUTOSAR_ECUC",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE": "true",
                "VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE": "false",
                "DEFAULT-VALUE": "false"
              },
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "name": "FrArTpTimeBr",
              "path": "/FrArTp/FrArTpMultipleConfig/FrArTpChannel/FrArTpTimeBr",
              "type": "ECUC-FLOAT-PARAM-DEF",
              "lower": "1",
              "upper": "1",
              "infinite": null,
              "description": "This parameter defines the time in seconds between receiving the last CF of a block or an FF-x (or SF-x) and sending out an FC or AF.",
              "metadata": {
                "INTRODUCTION": "It is obvious that FRARTP_TIME_BR + (FRARTP_TIMEOUT_AR * FRARTP_MAX_AR) < FRARTP_TIMEOUT_BS must hold (because the transmission duration on the bus has also to be considered). This parameter is defined in ISO 15765-2. It is contained in the configuration as a performance requirement.",
                "RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF": "ECUC_FrArTp_00044",
                "LOWER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "UPPER-MULTIPLICITY": "1",
                "SCOPE": "LOCAL",
                "ORIGIN": "AUTOSAR_ECUC",
                "POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE": "true",
                "VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES": "POST-BUILD VARIANT-POST-BUILD PRE-COMPILE VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE",
                "SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE": "false",
                "MAX": "65.535",
                "MIN": "0"
              },
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "name": "FrArTpTimeCs",
              "path": "/FrArTp/FrArTpMultipleConfig/FrArTpChannel/FrArTpTimeCs",
              "type": "ECUC-FLOAT-PARAM-DEF",
              "lower": "1",
              "upper": "1",
              "infinite": null,
              "description": "This parameter defines the time in seconds between the sending of two consecutive CFs or between reception of an FC or AF and sending of the next CF .",
              "metadata": {
                "INTRODUCTION": "It is obvious that FRARTP_TIME_CS + (FRARTP_TIMEOUT_AS * FRARTP_MAX_AS) < FRARTP_TIMEOUT_CR must hold (because the transmission duration on the bus has also to be considered). This parameter is defined in ISO 15765-2. It is contained in the configuration as a performance requirement.",
                "RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF": "ECUC_FrArTp_00046",
